  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 831,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Knee problem: was there TRAUMA? If so, what was the MECHANISM and how fast did it SWELL? If not, WHERE does it hurt?",
   "lines": [
    "every injury: history and exam first · X-ray to rule out a fracture (usually normal) · MRI only when the exam cannot decide",
    "TRAUMA, swelling within 6 h: anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) tear, fracture, patellar dislocation, large chondral injury",
    "TRAUMA, swelling after 6 h: meniscal injury, posterior cruciate (PCL) injury, high-grade medial collateral (MCL) sprain, arthritis flare"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_twist",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 194,
   "w": 484,
   "h": 62,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "TRAUMA: PIVOT or TWIST on a planted foot",
   "lines": [
    "no direct blow needed"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_blow",
   "x": 569,
   "y": 194,
   "w": 732,
   "h": 62,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "TRAUMA: A BLOW to the knee",
   "lines": [
